  "step_3": "The decision reason involves systematically overweighting outcomes with probabilities less than 20%, but in this case, the only outcome near that threshold is 0 Euros with 20% in Lottery A—just above the cutoff. The reason would not apply any adjustment. However, the individual’s report suggests attention to the possibility of avoiding further loss (0 Euros), which may reflect a psychological tendency to overweight the value of escaping a loss, even if not strictly due to low probability. The individual seems to focus on the 0 Euro outcome as a 'chance' to avoid going deeper into the negative, which aligns conceptually with focusing on small-probability positive deviations, even though 20% is not below the threshold. The decision reason is rule-based and technical (specific probability thresholds and weighting), while the individual’s reasoning is more qualitative and loss-avoidance oriented. There is a thematic similarity—attention to the possibility of a better outcome—but not evidence of applying the specific rule of adjusting probabilities below 20%. The individual does not mention probabilities, weighting, or comparative evaluation based on adjusted expectations.",
  "final_assessment_score": 30
