  "step_3": "The decision reason requires identifying outcomes with probabilities below 20%, increasing their weights by 10 percentage points, and then comparing the weighted sums. However, in this problem, no outcome meets the 'less than 20%' criterion—Lottery B's 20% outcome is not below 20%, so no adjustment applies. The reason would therefore not modify any probabilities. The individual, in contrast, mentions an 'unwahrscheinlicher minus', suggesting they are focusing on a low-probability negative outcome. While this aligns loosely with the general idea of attending to rare losses, there is no evidence that the individual applied the specific 10-percentage-point weighting rule or even identified that only probabilities below 20% qualify. The verbal report does not indicate any calculation or rule-based adjustment. The mention of an unlikely loss could reflect sensitivity to low-probability events, but it does not confirm use of the precise decision reason. The alignment is minimal and speculative.",
